    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "angle is the angle between the two directions, as bounds.position is defined",
    "speeds compare the longitude rate alone (no cos latitude factor, no latitude rate) with a central difference of +/- 1 minute of the reference without solar deflection (ephemeris only); the published bounds.speed is the angular rate difference hypot(dLonRate * cos lat, dLatRate), a different metric, so these show the bounds exceeded in longitude rate, not angular rate maxima; the true node's speed was not compared; the engine applies no deflection (docs/calc.md), so near conjunction with the Sun the difference from a deflected reference is larger",
    "the true node is compared with the ascending node of the osculating geocentric orbit of the DE421 Moon; the frame choice moves that node by several arcseconds, so its figure is definition-sensitive",
    "event times are absolute differences in seconds of TT; reference events are found independently of the engine"
